<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Mersal.ClinicalCodes</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Mersal.ClinicalCodes</AssemblyName>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <!--
    ICD-10 code handling, in ONE place. Design 44 §6 is explicit about why: the dot-normalisation existed
    twice — once in MasterDataNormalize, once copied inside PrescriptionValidator — and "two implementations
    of a matching rule will diverge" is not a prediction, it is what always happens. The divergence would be
    silent, and it would surface as an indication check quietly disagreeing with the catalogue that fed it.

    Dependency-free and I/O-free, like Mersal.Ingredients, so both the reference catalogue and the
    prescribing engine can reference it without either depending on the other.
  -->
</Project>
